IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VII "Benefit Repayment": ss 144 to 152. Piece ei4. Layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- Conventions as in ei4-part-vi-review.l4. In addition:
--   * Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a rate is a NUMBER fraction (30% is 0.3). Nothing in Part VII rounds: the rounding rule of
--     s 6(2) is "in this Part" (Part I) and does not reach Part VII (finding 5, asserted).
--   * The maximum yearly insurable earnings is an input: the published figure for the year is outside the text, and s 4 (the keel)
--     gives only the formula. Which year's figure is meant is fork F-ei4-12.
--   * "Income" and "taxation year" belong to the Income Tax Act, which is not among the inputs. The income figure is an input, and
--     the taxation year is taken to be a calendar year (fork F-ei4-13).
--   * The Part's own "benefits" (s 144) is the keel's s 2(1) "benefits" read without reference to this Part.
-- Hohfeld, for this Part: the Crown's claim to the benefit repayment is the claimant's duty to repay (s 145(1)); the Minister's power
-- to demand a return is the claimant's liability (s 146(c)); the claimant's immunity from the repayment when less than a week of regular
-- benefits was paid in the ten years (s 145(2)) is the Crown's disability to collect.

§ `Part VII -- Definitions`

§§ `s 144 Definitions`

-- "benefits means benefits under this Act, read without reference to this Part": the keel's s 2(1) "benefits".
-- src:2058 | benefits means benefits under this Act, read without reference to this Part; (prestations)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 144 "benefits" (src:2058)
GIVEN `the Part under which the benefits are payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 144 benefits` IF
    `s 2(1) benefits` `the Part under which the benefits are payable`

-- "income of a person for a period means the amount that would be their income for the period determined under the Income Tax Act
-- if no amount were (a) deductible under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z) of that Act, (b) included in respect of a gain from a
-- disposition of property to which section 79 of that Act applies, or (c) included under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6)".
-- So the deductions are added back and the two kinds of inclusion are taken out (fork F-ei4-16 on how far that goes).
-- src:2059 | income of a person for a period means the amount that would be their income for the period determined under the Income Tax Act if no amount were
-- src:2060 | (a) deductible under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z) of that Act,
-- src:2061 | (b) included in respect of a gain from a disposition of property to which section 79 of that Act applies, or
-- src:2062 | (c) included under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6) of that Act; (revenu)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 144 "income of a person for a period" (src:2059-2062)
GIVEN `the person's income for the period determined under the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act
      `the amount deducted under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z) of that Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount included in respect of a gain from a disposition of property to which section 79 of that Act applies` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount included under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6) of that Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 144 income of a person for a period` IS
    ((`the person's income for the period determined under the Income Tax Act` PLUS `the amount deducted under paragraphs 60(v.1), (w), (y) and (z) of that Act`)
        MINUS `the amount included in respect of a gain from a disposition of property to which section 79 of that Act applies`)
        MINUS `the amount included under paragraph 56(1)(q.1) or subsection 56(6) of that Act`

-- "Minister means the Minister of National Revenue": the keel's rule for Part VII.
-- src:2063 | Minister means the Minister of National Revenue; (ministre)
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 144 "Minister" (src:2063)
`s 144 the Minister for this Part` MEANS `s 2(1) the Minister for` `Part VII`

§ `Part VII -- Benefit Repayment`

§§ `s 145(1) Benefit repayment`

-- One benefit paid to the claimant in the taxation year: how much, under which Part, and for what reason. Only the Part and
-- whether the reason is a special-benefit reason are read.
-- src:2068 | (a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(1)(a) (src:2068)
DECLARE `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year` HAS
    `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
    `the Part under which the benefit is payable` IS A `Part of the Act`
    `the reason for which the benefit is paid` IS A `Reason for benefits`

-- (a) "the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year".
-- src:2068 | (a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year, and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(1)(a) (src:2068)
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 145(1)(a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN payment YIELD payment's `the amount paid`)
             (filter (GIVEN payment YIELD
                              `s 144 benefits` (payment's `the Part under which the benefit is payable`)
                          AND NOT (`s 2(1) special benefits` (payment's `the reason for which the benefit is paid`))
                          AND NOT (payment's `the Part under which the benefit is payable` EQUALS `Part VII.1`))
                     payments))

-- (b) "the amount by which the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings".
-- src:2069 | (b) the amount by which the claimant’s income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(1)(b) (src:2069)
GIVEN `the claimant's income for the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 4 (the keel) gives the formula; the published figure is an input
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 145(1)(b) the amount by which the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IS
    `the claimant's income for the taxation year` MINUS (1.25 TIMES `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`)

-- src:2067 | 145 (1) If a claimant’s income for a taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings, the claimant shall repay to the Receiver General 30% of the lesser of
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(1) (src:2067)
GIVEN `the claimant's income for the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 145(1) the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` IF
    `the claimant's income for the taxation year` GREATER THAN (1.25 TIMES `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`)

-- The repayment before the exception in subsection (2): 30% of the lesser of (a) and (b), or nothing if the income does not exceed
-- 1.25 times the maximum. "Nothing" is the text's own consequence (no repayment is required), so it is the number 0 and not a refusal.
-- src:2067 | 145 (1) If a claimant’s income for a taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings, the claimant shall repay to the Receiver General 30% of the lesser of
-- src:2068 | (a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year, and
-- src:2069 | (b) the amount by which the claimant’s income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(1) (src:2067-2069)
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year`
      `the claimant's income for the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` IS
    IF `s 145(1) the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `the claimant's income for the taxation year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`
    THEN 30% TIMES (min (`s 145(1)(a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year` payments)
                       (`s 145(1)(b) the amount by which the claimant's income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings` `the claimant's income for the taxation year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`))
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 145(2) and (3) Exception, and excluded benefits`

-- (3) "Regular benefits paid for weeks beginning before June 30, 1996 shall not be taken into account when applying subsection (2)."
-- The date is the Act's own (it is also the date the Act came into force, s 190(1), piece ei6).
-- src:2073 | (3) Regular benefits paid for weeks beginning before June 30, 1996 shall not be taken into account when applying subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(3) (src:2073)
`s 145(3) June 30, 1996` MEANS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30

-- src:2073 | (3) Regular benefits paid for weeks beginning before June 30, 1996 shall not be taken into account when applying subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(3) (src:2073)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 145(3) the week is excluded because it begins before June 30, 1996` IF
    `the first day of the week` LESS THAN `s 145(3) June 30, 1996`

-- The count form of subsection (3): of the weeks of regular benefits paid in the ten years before the taxation year, the weeks that
-- begin before June 30, 1996 are left out. The caller counts the weeks (reg 25, piece er2, says how many weeks were paid).
-- src:2073 | (3) Regular benefits paid for weeks beginning before June 30, 1996 shall not be taken into account when applying subsection (2).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(3) (src:2073)
GIVEN `the weeks of regular benefits paid in the ten years before the taxation year` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 2(5) and reg 25 (pieces ei-g0 and er2)
      `of those weeks, the weeks beginning before June 30, 1996` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 145(3) the weeks of regular benefits taken into account when applying subsection (2)` IS
    `the weeks of regular benefits paid in the ten years before the taxation year` MINUS `of those weeks, the weeks beginning before June 30, 1996`

-- (2) "does not apply in respect of a claimant who was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the
-- taxation year": zero weeks counts, one week does not (fork F-ei4-14).
-- src:2071 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of a claimant who was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year referred to in that subsection.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(2) (src:2071)
GIVEN `the weeks of regular benefits taken into account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 145(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the claimant was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year` IF
    `the weeks of regular benefits taken into account` LESS THAN 1

-- The benefit repayment, "an amount determined under section 145" (s 144): subsection (1), unless subsection (2) takes it away.
-- src:2067 | 145 (1) If a claimant’s income for a taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings, the claimant shall repay to the Receiver General 30% of the lesser of
-- src:2068 | (a) the total benefits, other than special benefits and benefits under Part VII.1, paid to the claimant in the taxation year, and
-- src:2069 | (b) the amount by which the claimant’s income for the taxation year exceeds 1.25 times the maximum yearly insurable earnings.
-- src:2070 | Exception
-- src:2071 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply in respect of a claimant who was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year referred to in that subsection.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 144 "benefit repayment", s 145(1), s 145(2) (src:2067-2071)
GIVEN payments IS A LIST OF `ei4 Benefit paid in the taxation year`
      `the claimant's income for the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of regular benefits taken into account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 145 the benefit repayment` IS
    IF `s 145(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the claimant was paid regular benefits for less than one week in the ten years before the taxation year` `the weeks of regular benefits taken into account`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `s 145(1) the repayment before the exception in subsection (2)` payments `the claimant's income for the taxation year` `the maximum yearly insurable earnings for the year`

§§ `s 145(4) and (5) Time for repayment, and limitation`

-- "(a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October in the year and before May in the next year": after October is from 1 November.
-- src:2076 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October in the year and before May in the next year, within six months after the day of death; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(4)(a) (src:2076)
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER   -- assumed to be a calendar year (fork F-ei4-13)
      `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` IS
    CONSIDER `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST death THEN death AT LEAST (YearMonthDay `the taxation year` 11 1) AND death AT MOST (YearMonthDay (`the taxation year` PLUS 1) 4 30)

-- src:2076 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October in the year and before May in the next year, within six months after the day of death; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(4)(a) (src:2076)
GIVEN `the day of the claimant's death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 145(4)(a) the last day within six months after the day of death` IS
    `add months` `the day of the claimant's death` 6

-- src:2077 | (b) in any other case, on or before April 30 in the next year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(4)(b) (src:2077)
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 145(4)(b) April 30 in the next year` IS
    YearMonthDay (`the taxation year` PLUS 1) 4 30

-- src:2075 | (4) A repayment must be made
-- src:2076 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October in the year and before May in the next year, within six months after the day of death; and
-- src:2077 | (b) in any other case, on or before April 30 in the next year.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(4) (src:2075-2077)
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 145(4) the last day on which the repayment must be made` IS
    CONSIDER `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 145(4)(b) April 30 in the next year` `the taxation year`
    WHEN JUST death THEN
        IF `s 145(4)(a) the claimant dies after October in the year and before May in the next year` `the taxation year` (JUST death)
        THEN `s 145(4)(a) the last day within six months after the day of death` death
        ELSE `s 145(4)(b) April 30 in the next year` `the taxation year`

-- (5) "For greater certainty, repayments under this section do not affect the determination under subsection (2) of regular benefits
-- paid": a repayment under s 145 never reduces the weeks counted. For a repayment not under s 145 the subsection says nothing: NOTHING.
-- src:2079 | (5) For greater certainty, repayments under this section do not affect the determination under subsection (2) of regular benefits paid to a claimant.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(5) (src:2079)
GIVEN `is a repayment under section 145` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 145(5) the repayment affects the determination under subsection (2) of regular benefits paid` IS
    IF `is a repayment under section 145`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2080 | (6) to (8) [Repealed, 2001, c. 5, s. 11]
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 145(6) to (8) (src:2080)
`s 145(6) to (8) repealed, and therefore not encoded` MEANS
        "(6) to (8) [Repealed, 2001, c. 5, s. 11]"

§§ `s 146 Returns`

-- "If a claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for a taxation year": required means the repayment is more than nothing.
-- src:2082 | 146 If a claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for a taxation year, a return in a form, and containing information, authorized by the Minister shall, without notice or demand, be filed with the Minister as part of the claimant’s return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146 (src:2082)
GIVEN `the benefit repayment for the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 146 the claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for the taxation year` IF
    `the benefit repayment for the taxation year` GREATER THAN 0

-- Paragraph (a): "dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year". The same window as s 145(4)(a), said in other
-- words (finding 6).
-- src:2083 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year, by the claimant’s legal representative within six months after the day of death;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146(a) (src:2083)
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` IS
    CONSIDER `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST death THEN death AT LEAST (YearMonthDay `the taxation year` 11 1) AND death AT MOST (YearMonthDay (`the taxation year` PLUS 1) 4 30)

-- src:2083 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year, by the claimant’s legal representative within six months after the day of death;
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146(a) (src:2083)
GIVEN `the day of the claimant's death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 146(a) the last day for the legal representative to file the return` IS
    `add months` `the day of the claimant's death` 6

-- src:2084 | (b) in the case of any other claimant, on or before the claimant’s filing-due date (as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act) for the year, by that claimant or, if for any reason the claimant is unable to file the return, by their guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146(b) (src:2084)
GIVEN `the claimant's filing-due date for the year` IS A DATE   -- out of range: subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 146(b) the last day for the claimant to file the return` IS
    `the claimant's filing-due date for the year`

-- Once the Minister has required a person by notice in writing to file (paragraph (c)), the day in the notice is the one that counts
-- (fork F-ei4-15). "Within such reasonable time as the notice specifies" is taken as the day the notice specifies.
-- src:2082 | 146 If a claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for a taxation year, a return in a form, and containing information, authorized by the Minister shall, without notice or demand, be filed with the Minister as part of the claimant’s return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act,
-- src:2083 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year, by the claimant’s legal representative within six months after the day of death;
-- src:2084 | (b) in the case of any other claimant, on or before the claimant’s filing-due date (as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act) for the year, by that claimant or, if for any reason the claimant is unable to file the return, by their guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative; or
-- src:2085 | (c) if the claimant or their legal representative has not filed the return, by such person as is required by notice in writing from the Minister to file the return, within such reasonable time as the notice specifies.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146 (src:2082-2085)
GIVEN `the taxation year` IS A NUMBER
      `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claimant's filing-due date for the year` IS A DATE
      `the day the Minister's written notice specifies, if the Minister has given notice` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 146 the last day on which the return must be filed` IS
    CONSIDER `the day the Minister's written notice specifies, if the Minister has given notice`
    WHEN JUST noticed THEN noticed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `s 146(a) the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` `the taxation year` `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died`
        THEN CONSIDER `the day of the claimant's death, if the claimant has died`
             WHEN JUST death THEN `s 146(a) the last day for the legal representative to file the return` death
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 146(b) the last day for the claimant to file the return` `the claimant's filing-due date for the year`
        ELSE `s 146(b) the last day for the claimant to file the return` `the claimant's filing-due date for the year`

-- src:2083 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year, by the claimant’s legal representative within six months after the day of death;
-- src:2084 | (b) in the case of any other claimant, on or before the claimant’s filing-due date (as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act) for the year, by that claimant or, if for any reason the claimant is unable to file the return, by their guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative; or
-- src:2085 | (c) if the claimant or their legal representative has not filed the return, by such person as is required by notice in writing from the Minister to file the return, within such reasonable time as the notice specifies.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146(a) to (c) (src:2083-2085)
DECLARE `ei4 Who must file the return` IS ONE OF
    `s 146(b) the claimant files the return`
    `s 146(a) the legal representative of the deceased claimant files the return`
    `s 146(b) the guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative of a claimant who is unable to file files the return`
    `s 146(c) the person required by notice in writing from the Minister files the return`

-- src:2082 | 146 If a claimant is required to make a benefit repayment for a taxation year, a return in a form, and containing information, authorized by the Minister shall, without notice or demand, be filed with the Minister as part of the claimant’s return of income under Part I of the Income Tax Act,
-- src:2083 | (a) in the case of a claimant who dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year, by the claimant’s legal representative within six months after the day of death;
-- src:2084 | (b) in the case of any other claimant, on or before the claimant’s filing-due date (as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act) for the year, by that claimant or, if for any reason the claimant is unable to file the return, by their guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative; or
-- src:2085 | (c) if the claimant or their legal representative has not filed the return, by such person as is required by notice in writing from the Minister to file the return, within such reasonable time as the notice specifies.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 146 (src:2082-2085)
GIVEN `the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is unable to file the return for any reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant or their legal representative has not filed the return and the Minister has required a person by notice in writing to file it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `ei4 Who must file the return`
DECIDE `s 146 who must file the return` IS
    BRANCH IF `the claimant or their legal representative has not filed the return and the Minister has required a person by notice in writing to file it`
           THEN `s 146(c) the person required by notice in writing from the Minister files the return`
           IF `the claimant dies after October 31 in the year and before May 1 in the next year`
           THEN `s 146(a) the legal representative of the deceased claimant files the return`
           IF `the claimant is unable to file the return for any reason`
           THEN `s 146(b) the guardian, curator, tutor, committee or other legal representative of a claimant who is unable to file files the return`
           OTHERWISE `s 146(b) the claimant files the return`

§§ `s 147 Estimate of benefit repayment`

-- src:2087 | 147 Every claimant or other person required by section 146 to file a return shall, in the return, estimate the amount of benefit repayment payable by them.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 147 (src:2087)
GIVEN `is a claimant or other person required by section 146 to file a return` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 147 the return must contain the person's estimate of the benefit repayment payable` IF
    `is a claimant or other person required by section 146 to file a return`

§§ `s 148 Responsible Minister`

-- src:2089 | 148 The Minister shall administer and enforce the provisions of this Part.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 148 (src:2089)
`s 148 the office that administers and enforces this Part` MEANS `s 144 the Minister for this Part`

§§ `s 149 Application of Income Tax Act provisions`

-- The provisions of the Income Tax Act that apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, for the purposes of this
-- Part. The Income Tax Act is not among the inputs, so the provisions are carried as data, in the words of the section.
-- src:2091 | 149 For the purposes of this Part, subsections 150(2) and (3), section 152 (except subsections 152(1.1) to (1.3) and (6)), section 158, subsections 159(1) to (3), sections 160 (except paragraph 160(1)(d)) and 160.1, subsections 161(1) and (11), sections 162 to 167, Division J of Part I, sections 220 to 226, subsection 227(10), sections 229, 239, 243 and 244 and subsections 248(7) and (11) of the Income Tax Act apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, except that, in the application of those provisions,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 149 (src:2091)
`s 149 the provisions of the Income Tax Act that apply for the purposes of Part VII` MEANS
    LIST "subsections 150(2) and (3)",
         "section 152 (except subsections 152(1.1) to (1.3) and (6))",
         "section 158",
         "subsections 159(1) to (3)",
         "sections 160 (except paragraph 160(1)(d)) and 160.1",
         "subsections 161(1) and (11)",
         "sections 162 to 167",
         "Division J of Part I",
         "sections 220 to 226",
         "subsection 227(10)",
         "sections 229, 239, 243 and 244",
         "subsections 248(7) and (11)"

-- The readings in paragraphs (a) to (d): a word of the Income Tax Act, and what it is read as. A word the section does not list
-- has no reading, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:2092 | (a) “Act” shall be read as “Part VII of the Employment Insurance Act”;
-- src:2093 | (b) “person” and “taxpayer” shall be read as “claimant”;
-- src:2094 | (c) “tax” and “taxes” shall be read as “benefit repayment”;
-- src:2095 | (d) “under this Part” shall be read as “under Part VII of the Employment Insurance Act”; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 149(a) to (d) (src:2092-2095)
GIVEN word IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `s 149(a) to (d) what the word of the Income Tax Act is read as` IS
    BRANCH IF word EQUALS "Act" THEN JUST "Part VII of the Employment Insurance Act"
           IF word EQUALS "person" THEN JUST "claimant"
           IF word EQUALS "taxpayer" THEN JUST "claimant"
           IF word EQUALS "tax" THEN JUST "benefit repayment"
           IF word EQUALS "taxes" THEN JUST "benefit repayment"
           IF word EQUALS "under this Part" THEN JUST "under Part VII of the Employment Insurance Act"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2096 | (e) paragraph 163(2)(a) of the Income Tax Act shall be read as follows:
-- src:2097 | “(a) the benefit repayment payable by him for the year as determined under section 145 of the Employment Insurance Act;”.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 149(e) (src:2096-2097)
`s 149(e) paragraph 163(2)(a) of the Income Tax Act is read as` MEANS
    "(a) the benefit repayment payable by him for the year as determined under section 145 of the Employment Insurance Act;"

§§ `s 150 Debts due Her Majesty`

-- src:2099 | 150 All benefit repayments, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a claimant under this Part and under the provisions of the Income Tax Act as they apply for the purposes of this Part are debts due to Her Majesty and recoverable in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 150 (src:2099)
DECLARE `ei4 Way a debt due Her Majesty is recoverable` IS ONE OF
    `s 150 in the Federal Court`
    `s 150 in any other court of competent jurisdiction`
    `s 150 in any other manner provided by the Income Tax Act`

-- src:2099 | 150 All benefit repayments, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a claimant under this Part and under the provisions of the Income Tax Act as they apply for the purposes of this Part are debts due to Her Majesty and recoverable in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 150 (src:2099)
GIVEN `is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a claimant under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an amount payable by a claimant under a provision of the Income Tax Act as it applies for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 150 the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` IF
       `is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a claimant under this Part`
    OR `is an amount payable by a claimant under a provision of the Income Tax Act as it applies for the purposes of this Part`

-- NOTHING for an amount that is not within the section: it then says nothing about how the amount is recovered.
-- src:2099 | 150 All benefit repayments, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a claimant under this Part and under the provisions of the Income Tax Act as they apply for the purposes of this Part are debts due to Her Majesty and recoverable in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided by the Income Tax Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 150 (src:2099)
GIVEN `is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a claimant under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is an amount payable by a claimant under a provision of the Income Tax Act as it applies for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `ei4 Way a debt due Her Majesty is recoverable`)
DECIDE `s 150 the ways in which the debt due to Her Majesty is recoverable` IS
    IF `s 150 the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty`
            `is a benefit repayment, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a claimant under this Part`
            `is an amount payable by a claimant under a provision of the Income Tax Act as it applies for the purposes of this Part`
    THEN JUST (LIST `s 150 in the Federal Court`,
                    `s 150 in any other court of competent jurisdiction`,
                    `s 150 in any other manner provided by the Income Tax Act`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 151 Communication of information`

-- The Minister's power to communicate; the claimant's tax confidentiality yields to it, to the extent the subsection says.
-- src:2101 | 151 (1) Notwithstanding subsection 241(1) of the Income Tax Act, the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, to the Commission, or a person authorized by the Commission, such information obtained under that Act as is necessary for the administration and enforcement of this Part and section 43 of this Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 151(1) (src:2101)
GIVEN `the information was obtained under the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for the administration and enforcement of Part VII` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for the administration and enforcement of section 43 of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is communicated to the Commission, or to a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 151(1) the Minister may communicate, or allow to be communicated, the information` IF
        `the information was obtained under the Income Tax Act`
    AND (   `the information is necessary for the administration and enforcement of Part VII`
         OR `the information is necessary for the administration and enforcement of section 43 of this Act`)
    AND `it is communicated to the Commission, or to a person authorized by the Commission`

-- src:2103 | (2) In relation to any information obtained under subsection (1), a person authorized by the Commission is an official or authorized person within the meaning of subsection 241(10) of the Income Tax Act and is subject to subsections 239(2.2) and 241(1) and (2) of that Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 151(2) (src:2103)
GIVEN `the information was obtained under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 151(2) the person is an official or authorized person within the meaning of subsection 241(10) of the Income Tax Act and is subject to subsections 239(2.2) and 241(1) and (2) of that Act` IF
        `the information was obtained under subsection (1)`
    AND `is a person authorized by the Commission`
